  "title": "Plans for Saturday (and Swahili Time)",
  "category": "time",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "level": 3,
  "order": 303,
  "theme": "friends",
  "culturalNote": "Swahili time starts at sunrise, not midnight. 7 a.m. is saa moja (\"the first hour\"), 8 a.m. is saa mbili, noon is saa sita, and 6 p.m. is saa kumi na mbili. The trick: add or subtract six from the clock time. Kenyans switch between Swahili time and English time (\"seven\") all day — when it matters, check which one someone means! A day trip to Lake Naivasha (90 km away) is a classic weekend plan.",
  "startingPoint": "Your friend Otieno calls you on Wednesday evening.",
  "grammarFocus": [
    "future-ta",
    "time-swahili",
